    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0528" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860F.01/524: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé to the Czechoslovak
                        Government in Exile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-21T00:00:00-04:00">March 21,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2128. With reference to your 3, March 17, 5 p.m. Czecho, you may inform Ripka
                    that the desire of the Czechoslovak Government <pb facs="0529" n="517"
                        xml:id="pg517"/> to enter into a civil affairs arrangement with this
                    Government is being taken under advisement, and we shall communicate with him at
                    a later time when it will be found appropriate to discuss the matter.</p>
                <p>Please so inform Phillips.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d456-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d456-f1" n="1" xml:id="d456-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably William Phillips, Personal Representative of President Roosevelt.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
